'' A WIDE ARGUMENT TO A BYREF STRING BUILT A NARROW TEMPORARY whatever the parameter
'' said, so a 'byref as const ustring' got an FBSTRING where an FBUSTRING belongs and
'' the call declined. The conversion is the parameter's FLAVOUR, not one flavour:
'' measured, fbc goes through fb_WstrToUStr and then the ordinary fb_UStrAssign.
''
'' A CONCATENATION HAS NO ADDRESS, so it is built into a wide temporary first and
'' converted from THAT -- 'G( w & "z" )' is fb_WstrConcatWA and then fb_WstrToUStr over
'' its result. The type test alone said no to it: a mixed concatenation has no type of
'' its own, which is why the wide-TERM predicate is asked as well.
''
'' THE WIDE TEMPORARY IS STILL LEAKED, as every wide temporary here is: fbc emits an
'' fb_WstrDelete for it and tiko-lang models no wide lifetime. That is a leak and not a
'' wrong answer, and rtl.bi's own header already records it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/ustring-wide-arg.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrConcatWA
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrToUStr
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrDelete
'' GOLDEN: expected/ustring-wide-arg.out
